<title>USA: Oakland, Calif., airport says cargo volume surged.</title>
<headline>Oakland, Calif., airport says cargo volume surged.</headline>
<dateline>OAKLAND, Calif. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oakland International Airport said on Friday that cargo volumes increased by nearly 12 percent in 1996 while passenger traffic remained flat.</p>
<p>The Oakland airport handled 1.36 billion pounds or 615,964 tonnes of air cargo, an increase of 11.85 percent for the year, the airport said.</p>
<p>Passenger volume totaled 9.73 million in 1996, a slight decrease, of 1.02 percent, from 1995, the airport said.</p>
